                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>President Truman and Winston S. Churchill, Prime Minister of
                    the United Kingdom, met in Washington January 5–18, 1952, to discuss a wide
                    range of issues of common concern. These discussions included consideration of
                    matters affecting the national security policy of the United States. For
                    documentation on the Truman–Churchill
                    talks, see <ref target="frus:frus1952-54v06p1">volume VI</ref>.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
